Hardware platform
-----------------

CMK is designed for and tested on the following hardware:

  * Microcontroller : Raspberry Pi RP2350 (dual Cortex-M33 / Hazard3)
  * Radio module    : Raspberry Pi RM2 (Radio Module 2) — pre-certified
                      Wi-Fi/Bluetooth 5.2 module based on Infineon CYW43439
                      - FCC ID: 2ABCB-RMC2GW4B52
                      - CE / RED compliant
                      - IC (Industry Canada) compliant
  * EEPROM          : ST M24M01-R (1 Mbit I2C, optional)
  * LED (optional)  : WS2812 / SK6812 chain driven via PIO

The reference variant ("Pico 2 W class") is also supported as the
RM2 module is the same Wi-Fi/BT subsystem found on the Raspberry Pi
Pico 2 W board.


Derivative work and code provenance
-----------------------------------

The CMK keyboard processing core (action system, keycode encoding,
process-record chain, layer engine, debounce, RGB / LED matrix engines,
WPM, send_string, eeconfig, bootmagic and the various process_*
modules under src/core0/) is a *derivative work* based on the C core
of the QMK firmware (https://github.com/qmk/qmk_firmware), which is
itself derived from the TMK keyboard firmware by Jun Wako.

